 Prophets of Rage with [a=Public Enemy]'s Chuck D and DJ Lord and [a=Cypress Hill]'s B-Real. After the announcement of RATM's return in 2019, Prophets Of Rage was disbanded, although the band's second reunion ended in January 2024.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:12212","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":6952,"name":"Tom Morello"},{"active":true,"id":64348,"name":"Zack de La Rocha"},{"active":true,"id":332379,"name":"Brad Wilk"},{"active":true,"id":420215,"name":"Tim Commerford"}],"namevariations":["R.A.T.M","R.A.T.M.","RATM","Rage","Rage Again","Rage Against Machine","Rage Againt The Machine","Ratm","The Machine Against Rage","レイ��・アゲインスト・ザ・マシーン","討伐體制合唱團","레지 어게인스트 더 머쉰"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/12212-Rage-Against-The-Machine","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.ratm.com","https://www.facebook.com/RATM/","https://www.instagram.com/rageagainstthemachine","https://www.threads.com/@rageagainstthemachine","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rage_Against_the_Machine"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/1694/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1694","image":"https://i.discogs.com/3g_7jbsnOYxlriCEahDmZyoQ0C38ouToBD3OCGXqYjI/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:403/w:318/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE2OTQt/MTU2NTM0MDQ1NC0y/NjY1LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/la0_Gwja4D-l5JqUEqriZNpzPwo4LWCsLwhJdwKR4HU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE2OTQt/MTU2NTM0MDQ1NC0y/NjY1LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"New Zealand-Japanese jazz keyboardist, music producer, composer, artist, and club DJ, born 16 August 1974 in Auckland.\r\n\r\nClive-Lowe's earliest recordings were made in 1991 with New Zealand urban-soul groups Sisters Underground and Select1. He released his first official album in 1996 as part of the group [a=Jazz In The Present Tense] on New Zealand's [l=Tap Records (3)]. He recorded two solo albums for the label in 1997.\r\n\r\nSubsequently, he moved to Japan, attended Boston's Berklee College of Music, and then spent several years based in London during the late 1990s to 2000s, working on several projects, including club nights, running label [l=Antipodean Records], much remix work, and releasing his own music across several labels.\r\n\r\nHe lived in Los Angeles in many years but in 2024 moved back to Japan. Whilst a jazz musician at heart, he covers numerous genres in contemporary music. In LA, he ran several club nights, including \"Church\" (also in NYC, DC, and Oakland), \"Scored\", and \"ETCetera\", and also the label [l=Mashibeats].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:1694","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":5229,"name":"12 Bit Rephugeez"},{"active":true,"id":8103,"name":"Homecookin'"},{"active":true,"id":13737,"name":"Kudu"},{"active":true,"id":21627,"name":"Tonkatsu"},{"active":true,"id":115115,"name":"Spacecadets"},{"active":true,"id":127135,"name":"JMJ Project"},{"active":true,"id":138431,"name":"Rain 4 Rent"},{"active":true,"id":140339,"name":"MusicLoveLife"},{"active":true,"id":148234,"name":"Nuvonesia"},{"active":true,"id":347722,"name":"Legends Of The Underground"},{"active":true,"id":412102,"name":"The Politik"},{"active":true,"id":477136,"name":"Freesoul Sessions"},{"active":true,"id":982890,"name":"Universal Sun"},{"active":true,"id":1342216,"name":"The Epicureans (2)"},{"active":true,"id":8569911,"name":"Rōnin Arkestra"},{"active":true,"id":9279580,"name":"Jazz In The Present Tense"},{"active":true,"id":11470835,"name":"Mark De Clive-Lowe + Friends"},{"active":true,"id":13731220,"name":"Bread & Souls"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["De Clive Lowe","De Clive-Lowe","De-Clive Lowe","M De Clive-Lowe","M de Clive-Lowe","M. De Clive Lowe","M. De Clive-Lowe","M. de Clive Lowe","M. de Clive-Lowe","M.de Clive-Lowe","MDCL","MDCL Aka Mark De Clive-Lowe","Marc De Clive Low","Marc De Clive Lowe","Marc De Clive-Lowe","Marc de Clive Lowe","Mark Da Clive Lowe","Mark De Clive","